  "[action] Wang Lung hears O-lan's voice.",
  "[says] (to Wang Lung) O-lan speaks about her dreams.",
  "O-lan (to Wang Lung): \"Dreams I have had of my childhood. Dreams of being carried in the arms of a man. Dream of being taken away from my father and mother and given into a man's house.\"",
  "Wang Lung (to O-lan): \"And did he love you?\"",
  "Wang Lung (to O-lan): \"Did he love me?\"",
  "O-lan (to Wang Lung): \"He gave me a little jade bracelet and a small jade pin. He gave me a new robe and gave me money. But he was angry that I had been bought by a man in a city.\"",
  "Wang Lung (to O-lan): \"And is it for that you would have had me drowned?\"",
  "O-lan (to Wang Lung): \"I was a slave, a kitchen slave, and I could not be sold to be a wife. I was sold, but I was sold as a slave to be a slave in the kitchen. And I was never given to a man. I was sold to be a slave in the kitchen. I was never given to a man.\"",
